ORGO.reg({"types":{},"items":{"exam-q3b-diagram":{"id":"exam-q3b-diagram","type":"energy-diagrams","role":"exam","kind":"mcq","diff":2,"src":"FA24 Exam 2, Q3B","fixed":true,"stem":"Which reaction coordinate diagram represents an exothermic {{SN1}} reaction?","choices":[{"h":"Diagram 1\n[[energy:R=0,TS1=22,I=12,TS2=16,P=-8]]","ok":true,"why":"Two humps with a valley between them (the carbocation), the first hump the higher one (ionization is rate-determining), and the products below the reactants (exothermic)."},{"h":"Diagram 2\n[[energy:R=0,TS1=24,I=14,TS2=20,P=8]]","ok":false,"why":"The shape is right for two steps, but the products end higher than the reactants: this is an endothermic reaction. The word exothermic was overlooked."},{"h":"Diagram 3\n[[energy:R=0,TS=20,P=-8]]","ok":false,"why":"Exothermic, but only one hump and no intermediate: a concerted reaction such as SN2 or E2. SN1 must show the carbocation as a valley."},{"h":"Diagram 4\n[[energy:R=0,TS=22,P=8]]","ok":false,"why":"One hump means one concerted step, not SN1, and the products end higher than the reactants, so it is endothermic as well."}],"solution":{"steps":[{"t":"Count the steps","h":"SN1 has an intermediate, the carbocation. An intermediate is a valley between two humps. One hump means a concerted reaction (SN2, E2). That removes diagrams 3 and 4."},{"t":"Find the slow step","h":"The first step, ionization, is the rate-determining step: the first hump is the highest point of the diagram."},{"t":"Read exothermic","h":"Exothermic means the products are lower in energy than the reactants. Diagram 1 ends below its start. Diagram 2 ends above it."}],"answer":"Diagram 1","rule":"Humps = steps, valleys = intermediates, end below start = exothermic."}}},"mols":{}});
